---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";

import config from "@/config/config.json";
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../old/components/Header.astro";
import Navigation from "../old/components/Navigation.astro";
import NavigationLink from "../old/components/NavigationLink.astro";

const pageIndex = await getEntry("privacy", "-index");
if (!pageIndex) return null;
const { title, meta_title, description } = pageIndex.data;
const {
  site: { base_url },
} = config;

// Build SEO object
const seo = {
  title: meta_title || `${title} - RocketSim`,
  description,
  canonical: `${base_url}/privacy`,
};
---

<style>
  main {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  section {
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;

    font-size: inherit;
  }

  .title--underline {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;

    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 2rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;

    list-style: initial;
  }
</style>

<Base seo={seo}>
  <Header title="RocketSim Privacy statement">
    Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy statement explains how
    RocketSim collects, uses, and protects your personal information.
  </Header>
  <Navigation>
    <NavigationLink href="/"> All Features </NavigationLink>
    <NavigationLink href="/for-teams">For Teams</NavigationLink>
  </Navigation>
  <div class="deprecated-grid">
    <div>
      <section>
        <p>
          <em
            >This privacy statement was most recently revised on 28 November
            2026</em
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          RNA Ventures B.V. (hereinafter: ‘we’, ‘us’ or ‘RocketSim’) offers
          services that allow customers to manage licenses, users, devices, and
          get insights into your statistics (hereinafter: ‘RocketSim Services’).
        </p>
        <p>
          These services are built around the use of a macOS/Swift application
          developed and offered by SwiftLee B.V. (hereinafter: ‘RocketSim App’),
          which is available for download via the Apple App Store.
        </p>
        <p>
          In providing the RocketSim Services, we process personal data. This
          privacy statement tells you what personal data we process from you and
          what we do with your personal data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-glance">
        <h3 id="privacy-glance">Our privacy statement at a glance</h3>
        <p>
          Your privacy is of great importance to us. We therefore comply with
          the General Data Protection Regulation (hereinafter: GDPR). This means
          that we:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Record our purposes</strong> before we process your personal data,
            as set out in this privacy statement.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Store as little personal data as possible</strong> and only the
            data necessary for our purposes.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Make sure that there is a valid legal basis</strong> for the processing
            of your personal data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Take the necessary security measures</strong> to protect your
            personal data. We also impose these obligations on parties who process
            personal data on our behalf.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Respect your rights</strong>, such as the right of access,
            rectification or erasure of your personal data processed by us.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="purposes">
        <h3 id="purposes">For what purposes do we use your personal data?</h3>
        <p>
          We obtain various types of personal data from you. We specify for each
          processing what personal data we obtain from you, for what purpose we
          process this personal data and for how long it is stored. If you have
          any questions or would like to know exactly what personal data we
          store about you, please contact us. Our contact details are mentioned
          at the bottom of this privacy statement.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="processing-data">
        <h3 id="processing-data">
          Legal basis for the processing of personal data
        </h3>
        <p>
          We are permitted to process your personal data only if there is a
          valid legal basis for doing so. This means that every time we process
          your personal data, we must evaluate whether we have a legitimate
          reason to do so. Without such a basis, we are not allowed to process
          your data.
        </p>
        <p>The potential legal bases for processing your personal data are:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Execution of an agreement with the data subject:</strong> we process
            personal data to fulfil the terms of an agreement we have entered into
            with you;
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legal obligation:</strong> in certain circumstances, we are legally
            required to collect and retain personal data;
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legitimate Interest:</strong> At times, we process personal data
            because it is necessary for a legitimate interest. In such cases, we carefully
            balance our legitimate interests against your right to privacy;
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Vital Interest:</strong> In exceptional and emergency situations,
            we may process your personal data to protect your life or the lives of
            others;
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Consent:</strong> Your personal data may also be processed with
            your explicit consent. We will only rely on consent as a legal basis if
            you have a genuine choice and there are no adverse consequences for withholding
            your consent.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Below, we provide a detailed overview of the various types of
          processing activities we may undertake.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="use-of-app">
        <h3 id="use-of-app" class="title--underline">
          <em>Use of the RocketSim App</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Purpose:</strong> To make it possible for users to download and
          use the RocketApp.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Personal data:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Email address</li>
          <li>Full name</li>
          <li>Device hardware ID (hashed)</li>
          <li>Device name (ie. Macbook of John Doe)</li>
          <li>Device hardware ID (irreversibly hashed)</li>
          <li>MachineCores (14 cores)</li>
          <li>MachineMemory</li>
          <li>MachineChip (CPU chip)</li>
          <li>MachineModelIdentifier</li>
          <li>WorkspaceName</li>
          <li>Scheme</li>
          <li>MacOS version</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Legal basis:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Execution of an agreement with the data subject;</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Retention period:</strong><br />During the subscription term,
          data will be retained. Upon termination of the subscription, all data
          will be permanently deleted within 30 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          Enterprise customers can disable Build Insights syncing from the Teams
          portal. When disabled, RocketSim no longer sends project names, scheme
          names, build durations, workspace lookups, or related machine metadata
          to RocketSim Services for Build Insights, turning the Mac app into a
          local-only app for that data. License activation and validation
          continue to communicate with RocketSim Services.
        </p>
        <p>
          Team managers separately control whether Build Insights data
          contributes to cross-team hardware benchmarks. Existing teams are
          opted out by default, while new teams can disable contribution at any
          time. RocketSim releases only anonymous aggregate results—hardware
          configurations, performance ranges, and sample counts—never team,
          workspace, scheme, device, or raw build-duration data.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="use-of-services">
        <h3 id="use-of-services" class="title--underline">
          <em>Use of the RocketSim Services</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Purpose:</strong> To make it possible for users to manage their
          licenses, users, devices and get insights into their statistics.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Personal data:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Scheme, project file name (e.g., MyProject.xcodeproj), and build
            durations
          </li>
          <li>Machine metadata, being:</li>
          <li>User credentials</li>
          <li>Team information</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Legal basis:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Execution of an agreement with the data subject;</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          <strong>Retention period:</strong><br />During the subscription term,
          data will be retained. Upon termination of the subscription, all data
          will be permanently deleted within 30 days.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="sso-authentication">
        <h3 id="sso-authentication" class="title--underline">
          <em>Single Sign-On (SSO) authentication</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Purpose:</strong> To allow users to authenticate through their organization's
          identity provider using Single Sign-On (SSO).
        </p>
        <p><strong>Personal data:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Email address</li>
          <li>Full name</li>
          <li>Email verification status</li>
          <li>Whether the user authenticated through SSO</li>
          <li>
            Authentication tokens required to establish, maintain, or terminate
            the authenticated session
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This information is received from the user's identity provider or
          generated as part of the authentication flow. RocketSim does not
          create or store a password for users who authenticate through SSO. The
          authentication flow requests the <code>openid</code>,
          <code>profile</code>, and <code>email</code> scopes.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Temporary session data:</strong></p>
        <p>
          State, nonce, and a PKCE code verifier are temporarily processed to
          complete the authentication flow securely. This data is deleted after
          successful authentication or when the authentication attempt expires.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Cookies:</strong></p>
        <p>
          A temporary, secure, HTTP-only cookie named
          <code>sso_session_code</code> is used to exchange the authentication session
          for access and refresh tokens. It is cleared after the exchange or upon
          expiration and is not used for advertising, analytics, or cross-site tracking.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Legal basis:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Execution of an agreement with the data subject or our legitimate
            interest in providing secure access to the services under the
            agreement with the user's organization.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Retention period:</strong><br />Account data is retained
          during the subscription term and permanently deleted within 30 days
          after termination of the subscription. Temporary session data and
          cookies are deleted after use or upon expiration. Authentication
          tokens expire or are revoked in accordance with the applicable session
          settings.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="online-sharing">
        <h3 id="online-sharing" class="title--underline">
          <em>Online sharing of flows</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          <strong
            >This section only applies if you choose to share a flow online.</strong
          > Online sharing of flows is optional and turned off by default. You turn
          it on yourself, you see a disclosure the first time, and you confirm a preview
          before anything is published. If you do not share a flow, RocketSim does
          not send any flow data anywhere. Opening a public flow link only shows you
          the page. It does not send flow data from your Mac, and you do not need
          RocketSim to view it. Flows are shared through flows.rocketsim.app.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Purpose:</strong> To let you publish a read-only snapshot of a flow,
          collect comments from reviewers, and keep your shared flows available while
          you use them.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Personal data we process when you share a flow:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Your email address (the owner email), which you confirm by link
          </li>
          <li>
            A public device key, generated on your Mac when you first publish.
            The private key stays in the macOS Keychain on your Mac and is never
            sent to us
          </li>
          <li>
            The flow content you choose to publish: screenshots, element labels,
            screen titles, and the app name, icon, and version. Screenshots show
            whatever was on screen, so mask anything personal before you publish
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Your steps and commands, parameter values, secrets, the bundle ID, and
          masked areas are never uploaded. Masks are applied on your Mac before
          upload, so we never receive the masked pixels.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Personal data we process for reviewers:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The email address a reviewer enters to comment, which they confirm
            by link, and an optional name
          </li>
          <li>
            The comments a reviewer writes, with the screen and element they
            refer to
          </li>
          <li>A sign-in cookie, see “Cookies” below</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The owner of the flow sees the reviewer's comments and who wrote them,
          by name or email address, in the email we send about new comments and
          in the owner view on flows.rocketsim.app. Other reviewers do not see
          them. A reviewer's email address and name are never shown to an agent:
          agents only receive comments the owner approved, under an alias such
          as “Reviewer 1”. Viewing a flow without commenting does not require an
          email address.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Website account:</strong></p>
        <p>
          Owners can log in at flows.rocketsim.app with their email address to
          see their flows. We process the email address and a session cookie,
          see “Cookies” below.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Cookies:</strong></p>
        <p>
          We set three cookies on flows.rocketsim.app. They are strictly
          necessary to provide the function you asked for, are only sent to
          flows.rocketsim.app, and are not used for advertising, analytics, or
          cross-site tracking.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>rs_session</code>: keeps a reviewer signed in on one shared
            flow after they confirm their email address. It lasts 30 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>rs_owner</code>: lets an owner see all comments on one shared
            flow after opening it from a link in an email or from the account
            page. It lasts 7 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>rs_account</code>: keeps an owner logged in to the account
            page. It lasts 14 days.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Technical data:</strong></p>
        <p>
          To prevent abuse, we apply rate limits per IP address. We store the IP
          address only as a hash made with a secret, which cannot be used to
          recover the address, and we clear these records automatically after a
          short time. Where you enter an email address on flows.rocketsim.app,
          Cloudflare Turnstile checks in the background that the request comes
          from a person and not a bot. Turnstile processes technical data such
          as your IP address for that purpose. Cloudflare, as our hosting
          provider, also processes IP addresses in its standard infrastructure
          logs.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Service providers for online sharing:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Cloudflare – to host the service and store shared flows in Western
            Europe, and to provide Turnstile bot protection
          </li>
          <li>
            Resend – to send confirmation, notification, and welcome emails
          </li>
          <li>
            Kit – to send email about getting started with RocketSim, see below
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These providers may process data outside the European Economic Area
          (EEA). We only do so if there is an appropriate level of protection
          for the processing of personal data.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Email about getting started with RocketSim:</strong></p>
        <p>
          If you confirm your email address to comment on a shared flow, we add
          you to our email list in Kit, with your first name if you gave one,
          and you receive an email with instructions to get started with
          RocketSim. If you register an account on flows.rocketsim.app, we also
          add you to Kit, so that we can send you email about RocketSim and see
          where sign-ups come from. Your welcome email after registering is a
          service email that we send through Resend. Every marketing email
          contains an unsubscribe link. Owners who only publish from the Mac app
          are not added to Kit. Confirmation and notification emails about your
          own flows are service emails, not marketing.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Legal basis:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Execution of an agreement with the data subject (owners who share a
            flow or log in to the website account, and the service emails about
            their flows);
          </li>
          <li>
            Legitimate Interest (providing the commenting function to reviewers
            on behalf of the owner, preventing abuse, and sending email about
            getting started with RocketSim, which you can stop at any time with
            the unsubscribe link).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Retention period:</strong><br />When the owner unpublishes a
          flow, or 30 days after the last activity on it, we delete its images,
          versions, reviewers (including their email addresses and names), and
          comments. Viewing the flow, commenting, publishing a new version, and
          renewing the flow all count as activity. We keep a minimal record of
          the flow (its id, name, status, and the link to the owner) so that the
          link shows the flow as removed. Finished Kit job records that contain
          an email address are cleared within 30 days. Owner email addresses and
          device keys are kept while the owner uses the service and are deleted
          on request. Subscriptions in Kit are kept until you unsubscribe. After
          you unsubscribe, the personal data is securely deleted within 30 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Your rights:</strong> The rights described under “What are your
          privacy rights?” apply to online sharing as well. You can ask us for access
          to the personal data we hold about you, or for its deletion, by sending
          an e-mail to
          <a href="mailto:support@rocketsim.app">support@rocketsim.app</a>. If
          you want a flow removed, or you want to report a flow, contact us at
          the same address and we will remove it.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="contact">
        <h3 id="contact"><em>Contact</em></h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Purpose:</strong><br />Establishing and maintaining
          communication with the users of RocketSim and/or other data subjects
          who contact us.
        </p>
        <p>For this purpose, we process the following personal data:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Full name</li>
          <li>Email address</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Legal basis:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Execution of an agreement with the data subject;</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Retention period:</strong><br />The above mentioned personal
          data shall be processed until the data subject unsubscribes from
          RocketSim's newsletter. Upon unsubscription, the personal data shall
          be securely deleted within 30 days.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="sending-newsletters">
        <h3 id="sending-newsletters" class="title--underline">
          <em>Sending newsletters</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Purpose:</strong> Sending newsletters to the users of RocketSim.
        </p>
        <p>For this purpose, we process the following personal data:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Full name</li>
          <li>Email address</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Legal basis:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Consent;</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Retention period:</strong><br />The above mentioned personal
          data shall be processed until the data subject unsubscribes from
          RocketSim's newsletter. Upon unsubscription, the personal data shall
          be securely deleted within 30 days.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Inform of new RocketSim features</p>
        <p><strong>Personal data:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Email address</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Legal basis:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Execution of an agreement with the data subject;</li>
          <li>Legal obligation;</li>
          <li>Legitimate Interest;</li>
          <li>Vital Interest;</li>
          <li>Consent:</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Retention period:</strong><br />30 days</p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="when-share-personal-data">
        <h3>
          <em>When can we share your personal data with third parties?</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          RocketSim will only share your personal data with third parties to the
          extent permitted by current legislation. We may provide your personal
          data to third parties when:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>We have engaged them to process certain personal data;</li>
          <li>We have a legal basis to do so;</li>
          <li>
            We are legally obligated to do so (e.g., if the police demand this
            in case of a suspicion of a crime).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Third parties processing personal data on our behalf or yours:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>MailGun – to send emails</li>
          <li>
            Auth0 (by Okta) – to broker SSO authentication between RocketSim and
            the customer's identity provider
          </li>
          <li>
            Cloudflare, Resend, and Kit – only if you share a flow online, as
            described under “Online sharing of flows”
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          RocketSim may provide your personal data to parties located outside
          the European Economic Area (EEA) to provide services. RocketSim will
          only do so if there is an appropriate level of protection for the
          processing of personal data.
        </p>
        <p>
          This privacy statement applies only to the services of RocketSim. We
          are not responsible for the privacy practices of other websites, which
          can be accessed through a link on our website.
        </p>
        <p>
          The RocketSim command line tool and RocketSim Agent Skill can be used
          with third-party tools and agents that you authorize. Any personal
          data or other information you share with those tools or agents is
          governed by their own privacy policies. RocketSim is not responsible
          for privacy practices or processing performed by third-party tools or
          agents you choose to use.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="secial-media-buttons">
        <h3 id="secial-media-buttons"><em>Social media buttons</em></h3>
        <p>
          We use social media buttons on our website that redirect you to the
          relevant social media platforms. This gives you the option to follow
          us and share content. You will also see advertisements on your social
          media page. The buttons operate through bits of code provided by the
          social media networks. If you want to know what the social media
          platforms do with your personal data, please read the relevant privacy
          statement:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://twitter.com/en/privacy"
              >Twitter (Privacy Statement)</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=nl"
              >Youtube (Privacy Statement)</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://bsky.social/about/support/privacy-policy"
              >Bluesky (Privacy Statement)</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="security">
        <h3 id="security"><em>Security</em></h3>
        Personal data security is of great importance to us. We therefore take appropriate
        technical and organisational security measures with regard to the processing
        of personal data to be carried out, against loss or against any form of unlawful
        processing (such as unauthorized access, corruption, alteration or disclosure
        of personal data). We constantly update security and pay close attention to
        what can go wrong.
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="your-rights">
        <h3 id="your-rights"><em>What are your privacy rights?</em></h3>
        <p>
          You can always contact us if you have any questions regarding our
          privacy statement. Besides that, you have the following rights
          regarding your personal data:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Right of access:</strong> you have the right to access the personal
            data we process about you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to rectification:</strong> you have the right to correct
            or supplement the personal data we process about you, e.g., if they are
            incorrect or incomplete.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to object:</strong> you have the right to object to the
            processing of your personal data and to direct marketing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to erasure:</strong> you may request us to erase your personal
            data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to withdraw your consent:</strong> if you have consented
            to us processing personal data, you can withdraw your consent at any time.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to data portability:</strong> if it is technologically possible,
            you have the right to have the personal data we process about you transferred
            to a third party.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to restrict processing:</strong> in some cases, you can
            request that we restrict the processing of your personal data (temporarily
            or otherwise).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may ask you for identification to fulfil your request. We require
          this information to ensure that the requested personal data belongs to
          the right person.
        </p>
        <p>
          We will generally comply with your request within one month. However,
          this period may be extended by two months depending on the specific
          privacy rights or the complexity of the request. If we extend this
          period, we will inform you in good time.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you wish to exercise any of your rights, you can do so by sending
          an e-mail to
          <a href="mailto:support@rocketsim.app">support@rocketsim.app</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="changes-to-statement">
        <h3 id="changes-to-statement">
          <em>Changes to this privacy statement</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          When there is a change in our services, we will also need to change
          our privacy statement. Please consult this privacy statement regularly
          for the most up-to-date information.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="questions-or-complaint">
        <h3 id="questions-or-complaint">
          <em>Questions or filing a complaint</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          If you have any questions or wish to make a complaint about the use of
          your personal data, please send an e-mail to <a
            href="mailto:support@rocketsim.app">support@rocketsim.app</a
          >. We will address each question and complaint internally and
          communicate this further with you. Should you feel we have not been
          able to help you properly with any questions about your privacy, you
          have the right to file a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection
          Authority (<a href="https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl/en"
            >Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens</a
          >).
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="contact-details">
